{
  "id": "baltic_island_castle",
  "title": "Baltic Brick Lake Island Castle",
  "description": "A fourteenth-century Baltic red-brick concentric fortress on a lake island: a square curtain with four corner drums, a twin-tower gatehouse, a tall central keep, and pitched-roof great hall, chapel and kitchen ranges around the courtyard, fronted by an approach ditch.",
  "style_id": "baltic_brick",
  "site_id": "lake_island",
  "prompt": "You are a Teutonic master builder raising a red-brick castle on a lake island. Lay out a compact concentric fortress: a square curtain of coursed brick with four round corner drums and a twin-tower gatehouse on the south side. In the centre raise a tall keep, and around the courtyard arrange a great hall, a chapel range and a kitchen range, each under a pitched roof. Cut an approach ditch across the south. Keep the brick curtains relatively thin, plumb and well founded, and make the gate passage passable.",
